projection, tracking project status and outcomes, and monitoring collaborative challenges. If needed, a Coordinator role supports this work. The
Team Lead may also work to educate investigators about best collaboration practices and ethical guidelines when working with quantitative
scientists. The Domain Science Unit Liaison who is part of the partnering Domain Science Unit plays a key role, assuming responsibility for
working with the Team to set goals and determine project prioritization. Importantly, this role also includes helping to mediate and resolve
collaborative challenges that arise in the partnership. The role of Liaison may also be shared between multiple individuals, in which case responsi
